Author: 仓鼠王 <yjianbin419@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 01:09:51 2026 +0800

    fix(frontend): a 403 says permission, not sign-in, and the screen's journey is the one submitted (ORD-0126 follow-ups)
    
    401 and 403 shared one classification, so a refusal the server explained by name
    (PREVIEW_GUARDED) was shown as "sign in again and your trip is there" -- rewriting a
    named HTTP answer into a cause a sign-in cannot fix, the same family as calling a 404 a
    network failure.  403 now classifies as FORBIDDEN with its own exit, and the attribution
    carries the server's own code so the sentence can quote it.
    
    The submit paths already take data.journey.id, but nothing measured it: the new node
    overwrites the stored reference with a different well-formed id and reads the uuid of the
    request the traveller's own next action produces.  killAB1 and killAB2 turn each arm red.

